8},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see the issue — all previous tests expected `{ premium }` without the 10% first-insurance surcharge. The spec examples clearly show that first insurance is included in all quotes. I need to update all previous tests to include the 10%.\n\nWait, let me re-read the spec very carefully:\n\n\"A first insurance carries a 10 % initial assessment surcharge.\"\n\nBut earlier tests say \"no modifiers\" — they show the base premium for a plain item without any special modifiers, just the raw value. These need to now include the first-insurance 10%.\n\nActually, looking at the integration examples:\n- Newcomer with cursed sword → 165 G: (100+50+10=160, +5=165). The 10 G is 10% of 100. So first insurance is on the base total.\n- Long-standing customer's second contract: 160 G: (100+50+30-20+10-15=155, +5=160). So 10 G first insurance still applied to the 100 base for the cursed sword.\n\nAlso looking at the test titles, tests like \"plain sword -- 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G (no modifiers)\" — the description says no modifiers,  base + fee. The spec examples show base without modifiers (like \"2 runes → 50 G base premium\"). So the test expectations should be adjusted.\n\nThe spec's integration example shows: newcomer with cursed sword: 165 = 100+50+10+5. So first insurance of 10% on 100 = persists.\n\nFor a plain sword: 100 + 10 (first Insurance) + 5 = 115. But the test descriptions earlier said 105. I got the test descriptions wrong in the test list. Let me fix the tests to match the spec.\n\nLooking at the arena again:\n> Premium modifiers:\n> - \"A first insurance carries a 10 % initial assessment surcharge.\"\n\nIt's actually a modifier, and the examples in the spec's examples section show the individual modifiers in isolation for clarity (\"Values shown are base premiums or raw payout amounts before integration with other modifiers, unless stated otherwise\"). But the integration examples at the end show the combined results with the 10%.\n\nSo for the \"modifiers → first insurance surcharge\" test, we need 115 (100+10+5). For the earlier base premium tests (plain sword, etc.), the examples in the spec show the \"isolated\" value not including the modifiers. But now that I've added the 10% always-on surcharge, all tests break.\n\nThe spec says: \"merely, each item in a `quote` is treated as a first insurance, regardless of customer history.\" So the 10% always applies to quote steps. Let me update the test expectations.\n\nLet me batch-fix all the failing tests. I'll update the expectations to include the +10\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_61f88498e9e04345b0a67b0c","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":6508,"output":651,"cacheRead":55552,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":62711,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950908759,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b2aa2b4c-9ed0-41a6-a3ed-9efe2a3da2f2","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_61f88498e9e04345b0a67b0c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote operation\", () => {\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it(\"should return premium of 5 G for empty item list (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for individual items ---\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain sword -- 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G (no modifiers)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain amulet -- 60 G base + 5 G fee = 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 65 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain staff -- 80 G base + 5 G fee = 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 85 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain potion -- 40 G base + 5 G fee = 45 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 45 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Components ---\n  it(\"should return premium for a single rune -- 25 G base + 5 G fee = 30 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 30 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 2 runes -- no block, 50 G base + 5 G fee = 55 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 55 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 3 runes -- block applies, 60 G base + 5 G fee = 65 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 65 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 4 runes -- no block (only exactly 3), 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 7 runes -- no block, 175 G base + 5 G fee = 180 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 180 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Mixed components ---\n  it(\"should return premium for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- no block (different types), 75 G base + 5 G fee = 80 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 80 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- two separate blocks, 2x60 = 120 G base + 5 G fee = 125 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 125 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: cursed ---\n  it(\"should add 50% risk surcharge for a cursed sword -- 100 G base + 50 G curse + 5 G fee = 155 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 155 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add 50% risk surcharge for a cursed amulet -- 60 G base + 30 G curse + 5 G fee = 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: high enchantment ---\n  it(\"should add 30% surcharge for a sword with enchantment 5 -- 100 G base + 30 G high enchantment + 5 G fee = 135 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 135 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add 30% surcharge for a sword with enchantment 7 -- 100 G base + 30 G high enchantment + 5 G fee = 135 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 7 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 135 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should NOT add high-enchantment surcharge for a sword with enchantment 4 -- 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 105 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: both cursed and high enchantment ---\n  it(\"should apply both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges to a cursed sword with enchantment 5 -- 100 G + 50 G + 30 G + 5 G = 185 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 185 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: loyalty discount (>= 2