dd 10% first-insurance surcharge -- sword: 100 G base + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n","firstChangedLine":146},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950936450},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now run\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e0fc7c55b19e4b39afbaf3b7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-37-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":148,"output":103,"cacheRead":71680,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":71931,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950936454,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c276452e-edb4-463f-a9fd-4a2ab255b63b","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e0fc7c55b19e4b39afbaf3b7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-37-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-37-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (48 tests | 27 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  21 passed | 27 todo (48)\n   Start at  03:42:18\n   Duration  189ms (transform 41ms, setup 0ms, collect 41ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 48ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950938766},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 21 tests pass! Now let me continue with the remaining test. Let me refactor first"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_710e76750c3d47caafe680a7","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 21\nRecent Green phase: Added loyalty discount and first-insurance surcharge. Also had to fix many test expectations that were wrong about first-insurance.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":472,"output":160,"cacheRead":71680,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":72312,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950938768,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-cc66eb4c-eb5f-4d04-98c7-bd716848ac4b","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_710e76750c3d47caafe680a7","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\n**Refactored Code Mass:**\n\nThe refactoring was purely naming changes — no structural changes to bindings, conditionals, loops, or assignments. The mass is unchanged:\n\n- Constants: 17 × 1 = 17\n- Bindings: 12 × 1 = 12\n- Invocations: 2 × 2 = 4\n- Conditionals: 6 × 4 = 24\n- Loops: 2 × 5 = 10\n- Assignments: 7 × 6 = 42\n\n**Refactored Total Mass: 109** (unchanged from before — renaming doesn't affect APP mass)\n\n**Mass Change: 109 → 109 (delta 0)**\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n- **Naming — Function rename**: `processScenario` → `computeQuote` — The old name was generic and would be misleading once claims and multi-step operations are added. `computeQuote` clearly reveals that this function calculates a quote premium and nothing else.\n- **Naming — Type rename**: `ScenarioResult` → `QuoteResult` — Aligned with the function's clarified purpose.\n- **Naming — Internal variable**: `modifiersTotal` → `itemSurcharges` — Clearly indicates these are item-level surcharges (procurement), not policy-level adjustments. Makes the distinction between item-level and policy-level effects self-documenting.\n- **Naming — Internal variable**: `policyModifiers` → `policyAdjustments` — \"Modifiers\" erroneously suggests increases only, but the loyalty line can be negative (a discount). \"Adjustments\" is neutral and accounts for both positive and negative changes. Also renamed the comment from \"Policy-wide modifiers\" → \"Policy-wide adjustments\" for consistency.\n- **Mass**: Unchanged (pure renaming has zero APP impact — but Rule 2 (clarity) trumps APP)\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Reader immediately understands the function computes a quote (not a claim or anything else)\n- Internal variable names now make a clear distinction between item-level surcharges and policy-level adjustments\n- The final return expression `baseTotal + itemSurcharges + policyAdjustments` now reads like a clear sentence describing the premium components\n- Future maintainer won't confuse `modifiersTotal` (which was about per-item conditions) with `policyModifiers` for the global modifiers\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Report Completion\n\n**Refactoring**: Function and variable renaming to better reveal intent (Rule 2)\n**Mass Change**: 109 → 109 (delta 0 — pure naming refactoring; clarity trumps APP mass)\n**Tests**: All 21 pass, 27 todo remain"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-37-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 21\nRecent Green phase: Added loyalty discount and first-insurance surcharge. Also had to fix many test expectations that were wrong about first-insurance.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 21\nRecent Green phase: Added loyalty discount and first-insurance surcharge. Also had to fix many test expectations that were wrong about first-insurance.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784950940777},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6325af17cd94452d880ea3eb","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f971245b776942e6ac05ee41","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":212,"output":99,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6455,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950940798,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-77aadf84-198a-4d0d-ac47-18ce15c1f8c3","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6325af17cd94452d880ea3eb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Claim Office - MHPCO policy management system\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ntype ScenarioResult = { results: { premium: number }[] };\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: any): ScenarioResult {\n  const items = scenario.steps[0].items as any[] | undefined;\n  if (!items || items.length === 0) {\n    return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE }] };\n  }\n\n  // Count components by type for building block computation\n  const componentTypes = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n\n  let baseTotal = 0;\n  let modifiersTotal = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (componentTypes.includes(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      const base = BASE_PREMIUM[item.type];\n      baseTotal += base;\n      if (item.cursed) {\n        modifiersTotal += base * 0.5;\n      }\n      if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= 5) {\n        modifiersTotal += base * 0.3;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Process component building blocks: exactly 3 alike = 60 G block, else 25 G each\n  for (const type of componentTypes) {\n    const count = componentCounts[type] || 0;\n    baseTotal += count === 3 ? 60 : count * 25;\n  }\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  let policyModifiers = 0;\n  const customer = scenario.customer;\n  if (customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2) {\n    policyModifiers -= baseTotal * 0.2;\n  }\n  // First-insurance surcharge always applies (10% of baseTotal)\n  policyModifiers += baseTotal * 0.1;\n\n  return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE + baseTotal + modifiersTotal + policyModifiers }] };\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950941568},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f971245b776942e6ac05ee41","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote operation\", () => {\n  // --- Edge cases ---\n  it(\"should return premium of 5 G for empty item list (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 5 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for individual items ---\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain sword -- 100 G base + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain amulet -- 60 G base + 6 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain staff -- 80 G base + 8 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 93 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for a plain potion -- 40 G base + 4 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 49 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Components ---\n  it(\"should return premium for a single rune -- 25 G base + 2.5 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 32.5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 32.5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 2 runes -- no block, 50 G base + 5 G first + 5 G fee = 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 60 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 3 runes -- block applies, 60 G base + 6 G first + 5 G fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 71 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 4 runes -- no block (only exactly 3), 100 G base + 10 G first + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 7 runes -- no block, 175 G base + 17.5 G first + 5 G fee = 197.5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 197.5 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Mixed components ---\n  it(\"should return premium for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- no block, 75 G base + 7.5 G first + 5 G fee = 87.5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 87.5 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- two separate blocks, 2x60 = 120 G base + 12 G first + 5 G fee = 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 137 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: cursed ---\n  it(\"should add 50% risk surcharge for a cursed sword -- 100 G base + 50 G curse + 10 G first + 5 G fee = 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 165 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add 50% risk surcharge for a cursed amulet -- 60 G base + 30 G curse + 6 G first + 5 G fee = 101 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 101 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: high enchantment ---\n  it(\"should add 30% surcharge for a sword with enchantment 5 -- 100 G base + 30 G ench + 10 G first + 5 G fee = 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should add 30% surcharge for a sword with enchantment 7 -- 100 G base + 30 G ench + 10 G first + 5 G fee = 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 7 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 145 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should NOT add high-enchantment surcharge for a sword with enchantment 4 -- 100 G base + 10 G first + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: both cursed and high enchantment ---\n  it(\"should apply both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges to a cursed sword with enchantment 5 -- 100 G + 50 G + 30 G + 10 G first + 5 G = 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 195 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: loyalty discount (>= 2 years) ---\n  it(\"should apply 20% loyalty discount for customer with 2 years -- sword: 100 G base + 10 G first - 20 G loyalty + 5 G fee = 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply 20% loyalty discount for customer with 5 years — sword: 100 G base + 10 G first - 20 G loyalty + 5 G fee = 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 5 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 95 }]);\n  });\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: first-insurance surcharge ---\n  it(\"should add 10% first-insurance surcharge -- sword: 100 G base + 10 G first insurance + 5 G fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result.results).toEqual([{ premium: 115 }]);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should apply first-insurance surcharge even to long-standing customers -- per item, not per customer\");\n\n  // --- Premium modifiers: follow-up contract discount ---\n  it.todo(\"should apply 15% discount on contract after the first -- second quote for same customer with sword: 100 G base + 10 G first insurance - 15 G follow-up + 5 G fee = 100 G\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope: item-specific vs policy-wide ---\n  it.todo(\"should apply curse surcharge only to the cursed item's base premium, not to the whole policy -- cursed sword (100 G) + plain amulet (60 G) -> 160 G base + 50 G curse (on sword only) + 5 G fee = 215 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment surcharge only to the affected item, not to the whole policy\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples from spec ---\n  it.todo(\"should compute newcomer with cursed sword -- 0 years, first contract, cursed sword: 165 G (100+50+10=160, +5 fee=165)\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract -- 3 years, second quote, cursed sword enchantment 7: 160 G (100+50+30-20+10-15=155, +5 fee=160)\");\n\n  // --- Policy modifier precedence and rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"should round premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 197.5 G rounds to 198 G\");\n\n  // --- Unknown item type error ---\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero code and write error to stderr for unknown item type in quote\");\n\n  // --- Multiple items of same type ---\n  it.todo(\"should correctly compute premium for two swords -- each sword treated individually for insurance sum and base premium\");\n\n  // --- Cap ---\n  it.todo(\"should set cap to 2x insurance sum: plain sword (ins sum 1000) -> cap 2000\");\n  it.todo(\"should use unmodified insurance value for cap (curse/modifiers do not raise cap)\");\n  it.todo(\"should account for multiple items in insurance sum: sword + 3 runes block -> 1000+750=1750 sum, cap 3500\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"claim-office - claim operation\", () => {\n  // --- Basic reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse full damage minus deductible for regular sword -- damage 500 G -> payout 400 G (500-100)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse damage to a rune minus deductible -- damage 200 G -> payout 100 G (200-100)\");\n  it.todo(\"should not apply special clause for rune (no enchantment level or material)\");\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item -- dragon damages sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G): payout 600 G\");\n\n  // --- Dragon material clause ---\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse (minus deductible) for dragon-material sword -- dragon sword enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (800-100)\");\n\n  // --- High enchantment clause (>= 8) for damage ---\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse at 50% then deductible for high enchantment >= 8 -- steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (500