tness if floating point creeps in. This is minor.\n\n### Rule 3: No Duplication\n\nThe most prominent duplication is item validation. In `Scen`:\n\n```typescript\n// Validate items (first time)\nfor (const item of items) {\n  if (!BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] && !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nAnd also inside `computeInsuranceSum`:\n```typescript\nif (val === undefined) {\n  throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n}\n```\n\nAnd inside `computeQuotePremium`:\n```typescript\nif (!BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] && !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n  throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n}\n```\n\nThe validation is done **three** in `processScenario`'s quote step!\n\n### Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n\n- The `quoteCount` in `processScenario` is only used to determine `isUp`. This is a minimal tracking mechanism — acceptable.\n- `UpdateResult` back is used as the result tuple but only in signatures, not internally — it's documentation-only. No harm.\n\n## Refactoring Plan\n\nThe most clear improvement is: **remove duplicate item validation in `processScenario`'s quote branch**. The validation is already done inside `computeQuotePremium`, so the extra loop in `processScenario` is unnecessary.\n\nThis:\n- Reduces code (fewer elements)\n- Removes duplication\n- Makes the code flow clearer (validation happens exactly once)\n- Still keeps tests green because `computeQuotePremium` already throws on unknown items\n\nLet me implement this ref"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3398d880d27c4e9486b8fae5","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items as any[];\n      const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n\n      // Validate items\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (!BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] && !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n        }\n      }\n\n      const insuranceSum = computeInsuranceSum(items);","newText":"    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items as any[];\n      const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n\n      const insuranceSum = computeInsuranceSum(items);"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":508,"output":1828,"cacheRead":12032,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14368,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784951064824,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-edf7d6d8-51dd-452e-b2e2-f5ff6c6b8060","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3398d880d27c4e9486b8fae5","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 105     if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n 106       const items = step.items as any[];\n 107       const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n 108 \n-109       // Validate items\n-110       for (const item of items) {\n-111         if (!BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] && !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n-112           throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n-113         }\n-114       }\n-115 \n 116       const insuranceSum = computeInsuranceSum(items);\n 117       const cap = insuranceSum * 2;\n 118       const premium = computeQuotePremium(items, customer, isFollowUp);\n 119 \n     ...","patch":"--- src/claim-office.ts\n+++ src/claim-office.ts\n@@ -105,15 +105,8 @@\n     if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n       const items = step.items as any[];\n       const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n \n-      // Validate items\n-      for (const item of items) {\n-        if (!BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] && !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n-          throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n-        }\n-      }\n-\n       const insuranceSum = computeInsuranceSum(items);\n       const cap = insuranceSum * 2;\n       const premium = computeQuotePremium(items, customer, isFollowUp);\n \n","firstChangedLine":109},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784951073264},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me run the tests to make sure they"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_089174b498794a1cb69f42f1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-37-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":311,"output":130,"cacheRead":14080,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14521,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784951073265,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0b3359ef-0fa6-4a27-91b7-1c99af32ef9d","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_089174b498794a1cb69f42f1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-37-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-37-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (48 tests | 20 skipped) 5ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  28 passed | 20 todo (48)\n   Start at  03:44:34\n   Duration  170ms (transform 41ms, setup 0ms, collect 41ms, tests 5ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784951074838},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 28 tests still pass. Let me verify the final state of the implementation"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3d832ecfb91d4d16a84c96ec","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":404,"output":64,"cacheRead":14336,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14804,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784951074838,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4206b368-f8b9-4338-9b69-4a7cfdd4fbeb","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3d832ecfb91d4d16a84c96ec","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Claim Office - MHPCO policy management system\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\n\ntype StepResult = { premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\n\ninterface Policy {\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  cap: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n  items: any[];\n}\n\n// Compute a single quote's premium (used internally by processScenario)\nfunction computeQuotePremium(items: any[], customer: any, isFollowUp: boolean): number {\n  if (!items || items.length === 0) {\n    return PROCESSING_FEE;\n  }\n\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let baseTotal = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] && !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      const base = BASE_PREMIUM[item.type];\n      baseTotal += base;\n      if (item.cursed) {\n        itemSurcharges += base * 0.5;\n      }\n      if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= 5) {\n        itemSurcharges += base * 0.3;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Process component building blocks: exactly 3 alike = 60 G block, else 25 G each\n  for (const type of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n    const count = componentCounts[type] || 0;\n    baseTotal += count === 3 ? 60 : count * 25;\n  }\n\n  // Policy-wide adjustments\n  let policyAdjustments = 0;\n  if (customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2) {\n    policyAdjustments -= baseTotal * 0.2;\n  }\n  // First-insurance surcharge always applies (10% of baseTotal)\n  policyAdjustments += baseTotal * 0.1;\n  // Follow-up contract discount\n  if (isFollowUp) {\n    policyAdjustments -= baseTotal * 0.15;\n  }\n\n  const rawPremium = PROCESSING_FEE + baseTotal + itemSurcharges + policyAdjustments;\n  return Math.ceil(rawPremium);\n}\n\nfunction computeInsuranceSum(items: any[]): number {\n  let sum = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const val = INSURANCE_VALUE[item.type];\n    if (val === undefined) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n    sum += val;\n  }\n  return sum;\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: any): { results: StepResult[] } {\n  const steps = scenario.steps as any[];\n  const customer = scenario.customer;\n  const results: StepResult[] = [];\n  const policies: (Policy | null)[] = [];\n\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n\n  for (const step of steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items as any[];\n      const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n\n      const insuranceSum = computeInsuranceSum(items);\n      const cap = insuranceSum * 2;\n      const premium = computeQuotePremium(items, customer, isFollowUp);\n\n      results.push({ premium });\n      policies.push({ insuranceSum, cap, remainingCap: cap, items });\n      quoteCount++;\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policyIndex = step.policy as number;\n      const policy = policies[policyIndex];\n      if (!policy) {\n        throw new Error(`Invalid policy index: ${policyIndex}`);\n      }\n\n      const incident = step.incident;\n      const damages = incident.damages as any[];\n\n      // Validate damages\n      for (const damage of damages) {\n        if (damage.amount < 0) {\n          throw new Error(`Negative damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n        }\n        if (!INSURANCE_VALUE[damage.itemType]) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type in damage: ${damage.itemType}`);\n        }\n      }\n\n      // Check item counts: each damage entry type must not exceed insured count\n      for (const damage of damages) {\n        const insuredCount = policy.items.filter((i: any) => i.type === damage.itemType).length;\n        const claimCount = damages.filter((d: any) => d.itemType === damage.itemType).length;\n        if (claimCount > insuredCount) {\n          throw new Error(`More ${damage.itemType} damages claimed than insured`);\n        }\n      }\n\n      const DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n      let totalPayout = 0;\n\n      for (const damage of damages) {\n        // Find matching insured item for enchantment/material info\n        const insuredItem = policy.items.find((i: any) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n        if (!insuredItem) {\n          throw new Error(`Item type not found in policy: ${damage.itemType}`);\n        }\n\n        let reimbursement = damage.amount;\n\n        // Dragon material: full reimbursement\n        // But if high enchantment (>= 8) also applies, 50% rule wins\n        if (insuredItem.enchantment !== undefined && insuredItem.enchantment >= 8) {\n          // High enchantment clause applies: 50% of damage\n          reimbursement = Math.floor(reimbursement * 0.5);\n        } else if (insuredItem.material === \"dragon\") {\n          // Dragon material: full reimbursement (already amount, no change)\n        }\n\n        // Apply deductible\n        reimbursement = Math.max(0, reimbursement - DEDUCTIBLE);\n        totalPayout += reimbursement;\n      }\n\n      // Cap enforcement\n      if (totalPayout > policy.remainingCap) {\n        totalPayout = Math.floor(policy.remainingCap);\n      }\n      totalPayout = Math.floor(totalPayout);\n\n      policy.remainingCap -= totalPayout;\n      const remainingCap = Math.floor(policy.remainingCap);\n\n      results.push({ payout: totalPayout, remainingCap });\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { results };\n}\n\n// Export computeQuotePremium for unit testing (renamed for backward compat)\nexport function computeQuote(scenario: any): { results: { premium: number }[] } {\n  const items = scenario.steps[0].items as any[] | undefined;\n  const isFollowUp = false; // unit tests use fresh scenario\n  const premium = computeQuotePremium(items || [], scenario.customer, isFollowUp);\n  return { results: [{ premium }] };\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784951075635},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good. Now let me calculate the APP mass changes for completeness.\n\n## Step 5: APP Mass Calculation\n\n### Before Refactoring\n\nFocusing on `processScenario` (the changed area):\n\n**Removed block** (the duplicate validation loop in processScenario's quote branch):\n```typescript\n// Validate items\nfor (const item of items) {\n  if (!BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] && !COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type)) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nComponent Count (removed):\n- Constants: `0` (2 occurrences of string literals in the template? no — `\"rune\"` and `\"oonstone\"` from COMPONENT_TYPES reference, not new constants) — actually from COMPONENT_TYPES reference, `BASE_PREMIUM` reference\n- Let me count the removed literals in this block: the `Error` string `\"Unknown item type: ${item.type}\"` has string literal before interpolation. So: `1` constant for `\"Unknown item type: \"` → but actually that's in all three validations, we're just removing one copy. Each removal removes that constant count.\n  \nActually, the constants are in the source text, not in the runtime count per-execution. Let me just count the elements in the removed code block itself:\n\n- Constants: `1` (`\"Unknown item type: ` template prefix — it's compile-time constant)\n- Bindings: `1` (the `item` in the loop iteration)\n- Invocations: `3` (`!BASE_PREMIUM[]`, `!COMPONENT_TYPES.includes()`, `Error()`)\n- Conditionals: `1` (`if`)\n- Loops: `1` (`for...of`)\n- Assignments: `0`\n\nRemoved mass: (1×1) + (1×1) + (3×2) + (1×4) + (1×5) + 0 = 1 + 1 + 6 + 4 + 5 = **17**\n\n### After Refactoring:\n\nThe code is simpler — the validation happens once inside `computeQuotePremium` and once in `computeInsuranceSum` (for the insurance sum case, which is needed for the sum calculation). The processScenario function no longer repeats the validation.\n\n**Mass change**: Removed 17 mass units.\n\nThe key insight: the duplicate validation was in `processScenario` because it used to need to validate before computing the insurance sum (which also validates). Now the flow is:\n1. `computeInsuranceSum` validates each item type (throws if unknown)\n2. `computeQuotePremium` also validates (it needs to for the premium logic)\n\nSo there are still two validation points, but the pre-validation in `processScenario` was completely redundant — `computeInsuranceSummary` runs right before `computeQuotePremium` and both validate. Removing eliminates one needless validation pass.\n\n## Step 6: Remaining Analysis\n\nLooking at the code, there's another potential improvement: `computeInsuranceSummary` internally validates items and throws the same error as `computeQuotePremium`. These two functions serve different purposes (one sums insurance values, one calculates premium) but both validate items. However, eresponsibility is inherent — the insurance sum must reject unknown items because `INSURANCE_VALUE[item.type]` returns `undefined` and the function needs to handle that. The premium function must also reject unknown items since `BASE_PREMIUM[item.type]` would be `undefined`. These are not \"duplicate\" in violation of DRY — they're both fulfi